{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 29 (S4 chapter 3, The Far Shores): low marsh isles on a shallow sea. The home isle (west) reaches the middle isle by an old causeway that drowns at high tide; tidal flats join the middle isle to the north and south isles at low water; a deep channel parts them all from the boat people's isle (east). Tides: high water until 40 s, then every 120 s the causeway and flats rise (40 s) and go under (100 s) over 8 s, with a message 10 s before each. The rival (aggressive, hard, maxTroops 14, maxPopulation 40, keepRaiders, worshipAfterSeconds 1500 so its own priests stay out of the hold) may build only dwellings, a warden lodge and Boathouses, starts with two Boathouses, two boats, six posted wardens at its boatyard and six posted wardens at its Hearth (the home guard keeps it standing through the hold, so the later destroy stages never finish at once on its fall). Until the player raises a Boathouse, four boat raiders land on the home isle every 150 s from 300 s (the idle loss; the bot never sees them). Staged: walk a warden along the causeway at low tide (reach); raise a Boathouse (build), which wakes three marsh stones (middle seer, north ley, south ward) and lands three raiders who pray at the north ley; from 100 s (south) and 165 s (north) after that, two boat raiders land on each isle every 200 s and pray the stones away until the hold is done (keepRaiders keeps them kneeling, so they do take stones and break streaks); hold stones on two isles at once for 150 s; that raises a dry road beside the causeway and a sandbar to the boatyard and posts six wardens and four firecallers at the yard; burn both rival Boathouses (destroy); then burn the rival Hearth. Mire breaks the landings. Bot win (offset 1) 23855: stages at 1416, 2413, 8011, 10363; across 13 bot offsets the win runs 18155 to 32442 (median 24223) and the rival survives every hold. Time limit 2700 s.",
